    },
    {
      "name": "Panel with Task Rows",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Panel-white container with hairline rows and round checks; olive when done.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2 class=\"ds-h2\">Anytime</h2><div class=\"ds-row\"><button class=\"ds-check\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Done\"></button><span>Sort out the loft</span></div><div class=\"ds-row\"><button class=\"ds-check\" aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"Done\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.25\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m5 12.5 4.5 4.5L19 7.5\"/></svg></button><span class=\"ds-done\">Pick up prescription</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font:400 16px/1.5 var(--font);color:var(--ink);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--r-panel);box-shadow:var(--shadow-panel);padding:24px 24px 16px}.ds-h2{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em}.ds-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:56px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-row:first-of-type{border-top:0}.ds-check{display:grid;place-items:center;width:28px;height:28px;padding:0;border-radius:50%;background:var(--panel);border:1.5px solid var(--ring);color:transparent;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .2s var(--ease),border-color .2s,transform .12s var(--ease)}.ds-check:hover{border-color:var(--ink-2)}.ds-check:active{transform:scale(.92)}.ds-check:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--signal);outline-offset:2px}.ds-check[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--olive);border-color:var(--olive);color:#fff}.ds-done{color:var(--ink-3);text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-color:var(--tick)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rail Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav",
      "description": "Rail items; the current item lifts to a panel-white key.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\"><a href=\"#\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8.5\"/><path d=\"M12 7.5V12l3 2\"/></svg>Today</a><a href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"5.5\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M4 10h16M8.5 3.5v4M15.5 3.5v4\"/></svg>Plans</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{display:grid;gap:4px;width:232px;padding:16px;background:var(--rail)}.ds-rail a{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:var(--r-ctl);font:500 15px var(--font);color:var(--ink-2);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color .2s,color .2s}.ds-rail a:hover{color:var(--ink);background:rgba(255,255,255,.45)}.ds-rail a[aria-current=page]{background:var(--panel);color:var(--ink);box-shadow:var(--shadow-key)}.ds-rail a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--signal);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Week Dial",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "dial-scale",
      "description": "Monday-to-Sunday tuning scale; orange needle on the selected day.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-scale\" style=\"--sel:5\"><button class=\"ds-day ds-past\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Mon</span><span class=\"ds-num\">26</span></button><button class=\"ds-day ds-past\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Tue</span><span class=\"ds-num\">27</span></button><button class=\"ds-day ds-past\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Wed</span><span class=\"ds-num\">28</span></button><button class=\"ds-day ds-past\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Thu</span><span class=\"ds-num\">29</span></button><button class=\"ds-day ds-past\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Fri</span><span class=\"ds-num\">30</span></button><button class=\"ds-day ds-sel\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Sat</span><span class=\"ds-num\">31</span></button><button class=\"ds-day\"><span class=\"ds-dn\">Sun</span><span class=\"ds-num\">1</span></button><span class=\"ds-needle\"></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scale{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr));border-radius:var(--r-ctl);background:var(--sunk);box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(28,29,31,.06) inset;font-family:var(--font);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-scale::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;top:0;height:8px;left:calc(100%/14);right:calc(100%/14);background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tick) 0 1px,transparent 1px calc(100%/24));opacity:.7}.ds-day{position:relative;display:grid;justify-items:center;align-content:start;min-height:76px;padding:22px 0 8px;border:0;background:none;color:var(--ink-2);cursor:pointer;border-radius:var(--r-ctl);font:inherit}.ds-day::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;top:0;left:50%;width:1.5px;height:15px;margin-left:-.75px;background:var(--ink-2)}.ds-dn{font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.02em}.ds-num{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink)}.ds-past .ds-num,.ds-past .ds-dn{color:var(--ink-3)}.ds-sel .ds-num,.ds-sel .ds-dn{color:var(--signal-ink);font-weight:600}.ds-day:hover .ds-num{color:var(--signal-ink)}.ds-day:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--signal);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-needle{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:calc(100%/7);height:26px;pointer-events:none;transform:translateX(calc(var(--sel,0)*100%));transition:transform .5s var(--ease)}.ds-needle::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:50%;top:0;width:2.5px;height:20px;margin-left:-1.25px;background:var(--signal);border-radius:0 0 2px 2px}.ds-needle::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:50%;top:16px;width:7px;height:7px;margin-left:-3.5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--signal);box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(229,83,26,.5)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Appliance Panel",
    "overview": "Life Organizer is finished like a mid-century household appliance: a warm light-grey housing, white panels set into it with hairline edges and a soft drop beneath, graphite ink for everything that is read, and a single signal orange for the things that point at now. Every part has one job. Nothing on screen is decoration: the only \"ornament\" in the system is the tick scale of the week dial, and that is an instrument.\n\nDensity is calm rather than sparse. Rows are 56px tall with hairline dividers, panels pad at 16px on the cover screen and 24px once their container passes 640px, and type stays in a narrow range (13px labels to 34px page titles) so hierarchy is carried by weight, ink tone and placement rather than size jumps. Numbers are first-class: times, dates and the dial all use tabular figures so columns of time line up like a printed timetable.\n\nThe interface is light by commitment; a dark, moody look is out. The system rejects the category default of grey-on-white with a blue accent, and the cream-paper planner costume.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm grey housing, near-white panels, graphite ink; one orange signal, one olive for done.",
      "Round keys for single-press actions (add, check, habit day); 12px-cornered rectangles for text controls.",
      "Soft, low, layered shadows with a white inset top edge, like a moulded part catching light.",
      "One self-hosted grotesk (Schibsted Grotesk) at weights 400 to 600, tabular numerals for all time.",
      "The week dial: a Monday-to-Sunday tuning scale with an orange needle on the selected day."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Signal Rule",
        "body": "Orange marks where \"now\" is and the single primary action on a screen; it is never a decorative accent, a heading colour or a panel fill. If two orange things compete on one screen, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Olive Means Done Rule",
        "body": "Olive appears only on completed state. Nothing else is green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Timetable Rule",
        "body": "Every time, date number and range is set in tabular figures so it aligns in a column.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Not Size Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy steps by weight (400/500/600) and ink tone (ink, ink-2, ink-3) inside a narrow size range. Don't add sizes above 34px or new weights above 600.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Moulded Part Rule",
        "body": "Raised things get a white inset top edge plus a soft graphite drop; pressed things move down 1px (`translateY(1px)`), and round keys also shrink to 0.97. Nothing glows except the signal key.",
